$CATEGORY: Vocabulary/HansenQuinn/1.2

::Q001::[markdown]the:{
	~%-100%ἐκεῖνος, ἐκείνη, ἐκεῖνο#Incorrect. **ἐκεῖνος, ἐκείνη, ἐκεῖνο** means “that” (Chapter 7).
	~%-100%ἀνάξιος, ἀνάξιον#Incorrect. **ἀνάξιος, ἀνάξιον** means “unworthy of ( + gen)” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%σοφός, σοφή, σοφόν#Incorrect. **σοφός, σοφή, σοφόν** means “wise” (Chapter 6).
	~%100%ὁ; ἡ; τό#Correct: **ὁ; ἡ; τό** → “the” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%ἐχθρός, ἐχθρά, ἐχθρόν#Incorrect. **ἐχθρός, ἐχθρά, ἐχθρόν** means “hated” (Chapter 9).
}


::Q002::[markdown]ἐκ + gen; ἐξ + gen:{
	~%-100%under (with motion)#Incorrect. **ὑπὸ + acc** means “under (with motion)” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%on account of#Incorrect. **διά + acc** means “on account of” (Chapter 3).
	~%100%out of#Correct: **ἐκ + gen; ἐξ + gen** → “out of” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%to the side of#Incorrect. **παρά + acc** means “to the side of” (Chapter 2).
}


::Q003::[markdown]δῶρον, δώρου, τό:{
	~%-100%small coin#Incorrect. **ἀργύριον, ἀργυρίου, τό** means “small coin” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%shield#Incorrect. **ὅπλον, ὅπλου, ὁ** means “shield” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%soldier#Incorrect. **στρτιώτης, στρατιώτου, ὁ** means “soldier” (Chapter 4).
	~%100%gift#Correct: **δῶρον, δώρου, τό** → “gift” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%road#Incorrect. **ὁδός, ὁδοῦ, ἡ** means “road” (Chapter 1).
}


::Q004::[markdown]μάχη, μάχης, ἡ:{
	~%-100%empire#Incorrect. **ἀρχή, ἀρχῆς, ἡ** means “empire” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%brother#Incorrect. **ἀδελφός, ἀδελφοῦ, ὁ** means “brother” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%citizen#Incorrect. **πολίτης, πολίτου, ὁ** means “citizen” (Chapter 4).
	~%-100%shield#Incorrect. **ὅπλον, ὅπλου, ὁ** means “shield” (Chapter 4).
	~%100%battle#Correct: **μάχη, μάχης, ἡ** → “battle” (Chapter 1).
}


::Q005::[markdown]εἰς + acc:{
	~%-100%under#Incorrect. **ὑπὸ + gen** means “under” (Chapter 5).
	~%-100%around#Incorrect. **περί + acc.** means “around” (Chapter 3).
	~%-100%with#Incorrect. **μετά + gen.** means “with” (Chapter 4).
	~%100%into#Correct: **εἰς + acc** → “into” (Chapter 1).
	~%-100%(of motion or measure) over#Incorrect. **ὑπέρ + acc** means “(of motion or measure) over” (Chapter 9).
}


